              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "owensmallwood"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "body": "Part of the global search index work, tracked in grafana/search-and-storage-team#1022.\n\nBefore, an index could count its documents or rank a page of them. Neither tells you which objects are present and at which version, which is what you need to compare an index with storage. Now `ResourceIndex.ListDocumentRefs(ctx, groupResource)` lists the live documents of one resource type, each as a name and the version it was indexed at.\n\n- **The name comes from the document id,** which every document has, rather than from a field a document could be missing.\n- **The version comes from the stored string copy,** because resource versions are too large to survive bleve's float64 numbers. A document whose version can't be read is reported with zero, so a caller treats it as out of date rather than skipping it.\n- **Results are paged by document id,** which is unique, so a page boundary can't repeat or skip a document.\n- **Asking for the wrong type is an error:** another type on a per-resource index, or a type a global index doesn't cover. An empty answer would look like every document had been deleted.\n\nNothing calls it yet. Its first user is the per-type sync that will replace the global index's full rebuilds on coverage changes and imports.\n"
    },
