              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "RafaelPaulovic"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "body": "Reading a resource with an invalid name (for example `GET /dashboards/{name}` with a name containing a space) returned 500 from unified storage. `server.Read` skips name validation on purpose, but the KV backend validates the name when looking up the key and returns an error that `ReadResource` turned into a 500. This burned part of the Provisioning API SLO.\n\n`ReadResource` and `BatchReadResource` in the KV backend now return 400 for invalid names. The existing \"too large resource version\" 400 is still checked first.\n\nWe return 400 rather than 404 because name validation has been made stricter in the past. A 404 would say that an object doesn't exist, when the real problem is its name.\n\nThe SQL backend does not validate names on read and still returns 404 for these names. That difference existed before; this change only removes the 500.\n\nRelated: #133690\n"
    },
