      },
      "body": "## Description\r\n<!--- A high level description of what this PR is doing -->\r\nSignal explorer metric search only filtered the names loaded when the card opened, which the datasource series limit cuts off on large datasources, so metrics the query editor finds were missing. When the loaded catalog may be incomplete, search now asks the datasource for matching names, as the query editor does. Fixes #132819.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n<!--- Describe your changes in detail -->\r\n* `fetchCatalog` reports whether the catalog is truncated: the labels endpoint returning `seriesLimit` names, or any datasource on the series endpoint or search API, whose name lists can't be shown to be complete. Datasources with metrics lookup disabled are never treated as truncated, so they send no search requests.\r\n* New `searchCatalog` queries `__name__` values with a case-insensitive, regex-escaped `{__name__=~\"(?i).*term.*\"}` matcher, cached like the other lookups and capped at 20 terms.\r\n* `useMetricCatalog` keeps filtering in the browser when the catalog is complete, and otherwise runs a 300 ms debounced server search while narrowing the last results by the live term. Clearing the box restores the full catalog immediately.\r\n* `useAsyncResource` accepts a `null` key meaning \"no request\".\r\n\r\n## Risks\r\n<!--- Describe what risks you've considered i.e. what features are most likely to break -->\r\nDatasources on the series endpoint or search API now send one debounced request per search term instead of filtering locally. Search results for names outside the catalog may carry less metadata (type and help) if the metadata endpoint was also truncated.\r\n\r\n## Demo\r\n<!--- Attach a demo gif/video or screenshots of the changes if applicable -->\r\nN/A\r\n\r\n## Testing Instructions\r\n<!--- Provide step by step instructions and the dashboard if applicable -->\r\n* Open Explore with a Prometheus datasource that has more metric names than its series limit (default 40,000), or lower the datasource's series limit below its metric count.\r\n* Open the Datasource explorer sidebar and search for a metric the query editor's metric picker finds but the unfiltered sidebar list doesn't show; it should now appear.\r\n* On a small datasource, confirm typing in the sidebar search sends no `label/__name__/values` requests.\r\n\r\n## Reviewer Checklist\r\n<!--- The reviewer should make sure the following has been done -->\r\n- [ ] Tests are added where applicable\r\n- [ ] Issue is linked to PR\r\n- [ ] Code pulled and tested\r\n- [ ] Code is meaningfully improved if applicable\r\n\r\nClose DPRO-388"
    },
