      "body": "The Recently deleted page shows no date for any dashboard. It has since #120790 removed the old search path in April — the only thing that ever produced `permanentlyDeleteDate`, the field the results table column reads. The column has been dead code since.\n\nThe value was there all along: both the trash endpoint and the older listing path put the deletion time into `deletionTimestamp`, and the page already sorts on it. The column now reads that field and shows the deletion date.\n\n\"Time remaining\" goes away with it, because how long is left depends on the retention window, which lives in server config the browser does not have.\n\nDeleted results now always carry the field, even when empty, since the table derives its columns from the first row. An item with no deletion time shows a dash and sorts last.\n\nFound while investigating a support escalation where a customer reported missing deletion timestamps — the data was in the API response, only the display was missing.\n"
    }
